Subject: Cantor In-Memory Source Excerpt P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] e9e31881-76c2-4224-8a04-4adec69f702c
@ [specification_uuid] adbc4a74-c340-4e39-bec6-f199285052b9

& [Need]
  + semantic find identifies a governed unit but cannot yet show the exact supplied declaration bytes that justify the hit
  + exact source recovery is the smallest auditability bridge toward a usable Cantor host and requires no ambient host or storage authority

& [Choice]
  + reuse sealed supplied project values and semantic spans rather than port the SQLite Reader or host project loader
  + centralize complete ProjectAssemblyResult replay in cantor_sop_project so query and excerpt consume one reviewed validation rule
  + preserve unknown-record and known-source-unavailable as distinct typed refusals

& [Tradeoff]
  + P0 returns one exact record excerpt and deliberately omits batch closure context windows highlighting ranking and references
  + embedding caller-owned project values costs memory but maintains deterministic provider-free proof and avoids premature persistence

& [Authority]
  + implementation authority is limited to CISE-001 through CISE-022 and CISE-A01 through CISE-A05
